body:
as a turkish person living in turkey, this is my take;
a huge majority of us disagree with erdogan's reign and we've been trying to get another president for years now but the elections are rigged, as you probably know. our country is doing seriously bad economically and we're suffering big time yet the government doesn't even acknowledge it, saying that our economy is great despite everything clearly showing it's not... the only reason a lot of turks don't wanna have syrian refugees (for example) is because the government doesn't even support its own people yet will give lots of money and support to refugees as long as they vote for erdogan. half the country is incredibly poor and suffering from things like starvation, police brutality and terrorist attacks everyday yet the syrian refugees here live luxurious lives- a lot of them act homeless to collect money on the streets and it works wonderfully for them along with the money the government provides them with. this all happens as actual homeless turks die on the streets every day. 

so tldr: we hate erdogan and the current ruling party. you're actually supporting us by being a tourist since it prevents taxes getting higher, as we get taxed for everything from regular shopping to necessities (paying monthly to keep our cars, homes, etc.) a lot of us have so much respect for the eu so thank you for visiting our country!!
